{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P11560", "secondaryAccessions": ["D9PY33"], "uniProtkbId": "MCRB_METTM", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1989-10-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-01-28", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2007-01-23", "entryVersion": 148, "sequenceVersion": 3}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Methanothermobacter marburgensis (strain ATCC BAA-927 / DSM 2133 / JCM 14651 / NBRC 100331 / OCM 82 / Marburg)", "commonName": "Methanobacterium thermoautotrophicum", "taxonId": 79929, "lineage": ["Archaea", "Methanobacteriati", "Methanobacteriota", "Methanomada group", "Methanobacteria", "Methanobacteriales", "Methanobacteriaceae", "Methanothermobacter"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}], "value": "Methyl-coenzyme M reductase I subunit beta"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}], "value": "MCR I beta"}], "ecNumbers": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25691570"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27140643"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}], "value": "2.8.4.1"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Coenzyme-B sulfoethylthiotransferase beta"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "mcrB"}, "orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "MTBMA_c15520"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}], "value": "Component of the methyl-coenzyme M reductase (MCR) I that catalyzes the reductive cleavage of methyl-coenzyme M (CoM-S-CH3 or 2-(methylthio)ethanesulfonate) using coenzyme B (CoB or 7-mercaptoheptanoylthreonine phosphate) as reductant which results in the production of methane and the mixed heterodisulfide of CoB and CoM (CoM-S-S-CoB). This is the final step in methanogenesis (PubMed:2269306, PubMed:3350018). Neither N-6-mercaptohexanoylthreonine phosphate (H-S-HxoTP) nor N-8-mercaptooctanoylthreonine phosphate (H-SOcoTP) nor any other thiol compound such as CoA or CoM can substitute for CoB as the electron donor (PubMed:3350018)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "coenzyme B + methyl-coenzyme M = methane + coenzyme M-coenzyme B heterodisulfide", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:12532"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:16183"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:58286"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:58411"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:58596"}], "ecNumber": "2.8.4.1", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25691570"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27140643"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}]}, "physiologicalReactions": [{"directionType": "left-to-right", "reactionCrossReference": {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:12533"}, "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27140643"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}]}]}, {"commentType": "COFACTOR", "cofactors": [{"name": "coenzyme F430", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9030728"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9367957"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:60540"}}], "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9030728"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9367957"}], "value": "Binds 2 coenzyme F430 non-covalently per MCR complex. Coenzyme F430 is a yellow nickel porphinoid (PubMed:3350018, PubMed:9367957). Methyl-coenzyme-M reductase is activated when the enzyme-bound coenzyme F430 is reduced to the Ni(I) oxidation state (PubMed:9030728)."}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27140643"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}], "value": "Methyl-coenzyme M reductase activity is inhibited by 3-nitrooxypropanol (3-NOP) in vitro and in vivo, by oxidation of its active site Ni(I), which stops both growth and methanogenesis (PubMed:27140643). Is also inhibited by the reaction product CoM-S-S-CoB (PubMed:3350018)"}], "commentType": "ACTIVITY REGULATION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27140643"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}], "value": "One-carbon metabolism; methyl-coenzyme M reduction; methane from methyl-coenzyme M: step 1/1"}], "commentType": "PATHWAY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "3350018"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9367957"}], "value": "MCR is a hexamer of two alpha, two beta, and two gamma chains, forming a dimer of heterotrimers"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23533332"}], "value": "Under growth limiting conditions on nickel-depleted media, a fraction of 70% of the enzyme is localized close to the cytoplasmic membrane, which implies 'facultative' membrane association of the enzyme"}]}, "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "23533332"}], "value": "Cytoplasm", "id": "SL-0086"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}], "value": "There are two MCR complexes in this bacteria. MCR II is expressed in the early growth phase. Late growth cells contain mostly MCR I"}], "commentType": "DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25691570"}], "value": "The MCR reaction has been shown to follow an ordered bi-bi ternary complex mechanism, in which methyl-SCoM must enter the MCR active site prior to CoB for a productive catalysis"}], "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the methyl-coenzyme M reductase beta subunit family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Initiator methionine", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Removed", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "2269306"}]}, {"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 2, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 443, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Methyl-coenzyme M reductase I subunit beta", "featureId": "PRO_0000147468"}, {"type": "Binding site", "location": {"start": {"value": 367, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 367, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "", "featureCrossReferences": [{"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:58319"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11491299"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "20707311"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21438550"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "27467699"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9367957"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0007744", "source": "PDB", "id": "1HBN"}, {"evidenceCode": "E